    description: "WHAT. Two analyzers and one shared helper decide whether a resolver match is strong by comparing\nLookupResult.match_type against the pair (\"exact\", \"path_hint\"): analyze/base.py defer_bare_method_call, and\ngo.py:1016. `caller_file` (the one candidate defined in the caller's own file, added by WI-jomik) is in neither\ncopy, so a bare call whose only same-named candidate in the caller's file is a method of ANOTHER class is treated\nas a weak match and deferred, while kotlin.py:2852 separately rewrites an `exact` hit with no import behind it to\n`suffix` before asking. Nobody decided whether `caller_file` is strong evidence for a cross-class method.\n\nFOUND BY audit docs/audits/0030 (2026-11-25), silent bug 4. NOT EXAMINED: whether the current behaviour is right;\nno fixture was run. The vocabulary itself (seven values declared only in a docstring) gets constants with the\nresolution mark; this item is the question the constants do not answer.\n\nDONE WHEN the strong set is declared once in symbol_resolution.py beside the constants, both copies read it, and a\ntest states, with a fixture per value, which match types bind a bare call to another class's method."  # feb7
